WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.836
-The President is accusing
Democrats of treason

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.405
as Republicans flail

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.206
in their attempts to
defend him from impeachment.

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:10.009
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:14.280
♪♪

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.183
After more than two years
of serially abusing his power

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.819
as president, using the office
to enrich himself,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.321
welcoming the interference
of foreign governments,

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.758
and inflicting human-rights
abuses on migrant families,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.527
Donald Trump probably thought
he got away with all of it.

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.229
He was like Patrick Swayze
at the end of "Point Break,"

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:32.098
except instead of
a cool-ass surfer,

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.600
he looks like a guy
who tried to hide a huge wave,

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.370
fell off his board, and then
just washed up on the beach.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.838
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.474
This afternoon, Trump spoke to
the media in the Oval Office,

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:44.077
and you can tell he's totally
out of ways to defend himself

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.945
because now
he just keeps insisting

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.480
that he didn't do anything wrong

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.649
on his call
with the president of Ukraine.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.050
-We have a whistleblower

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.919
that reports things
that were incorrect.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:56.088
As you know -- and you probably
now have figured it out --

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:59.492
the statement I made
to the president of Ukraine --

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:03.295
a good man, a nice man, new --
was perfect.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:05.097
It was perfect.

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.265
-I like how he just throws in,

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:07.733
"You probably have
figured it out,"

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.001
like they're all on his side.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:11.036
Like, in Trump's mind,
reporters are out there

00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:12.906
pounding the pavement,
digging for clues,

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.574
marching into their
editor's office going,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.042
"Chief, I got the scoop
of the year.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.512
Put it on the front page.
The call was perfect."

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.880
Now reality
is catching up with Trump

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.217
as Democrats move forward with
their impeachment inquiry

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.352
and support for impeachment
rises in the polls.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.021
And in response to all that,

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.356
Trump is predictably
losing his mind.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.059
-The President leading his own
defense on Twitter overnight

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.827
lashing out,
saying that Adam Schiff

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.895
should be tried for treason,
even suggesting

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:39.065
the possibility of civil war
if he's impeached.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.968
-Trump even quotes
a Fox News guest who predicted

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.337
a "Civil War-like fracture"
would result from the inquiry

00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:47.306
and calls for Chairman Schiff
to resign.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:51.077
-"In addition, I want to meet
not only my accuser,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.445
who presented second-
and third-hand information,

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:56.716
but also the person who
illegally gave this information,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.552
which was largely incorrect,
to the whistleblower.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.955
Was this person spying
on the U.S. president?

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.657
Big consequences."

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.059
-"Representative Adam Schiff

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.427
illegally made up a fake
and terrible statement

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:10.095
pretended it to be mine

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:13.265
as the most important part of my
call to the Ukrainian president,

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:15.801
and read it aloud to Congress
and the American people.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:19.004
It bore no relationship
to what I said on the call.

00:02:19.004 --> 00:02:20.840
Arrest for Treason?"

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.875
-Honestly,
thank God he's a moron.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.344
He's threatening the collapse
of American democracy,

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.046
and he says it like
he's offering

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.314
hors d'oeuvres at a party.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.382
"Can I get you
a bacon-wrapped dates?

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.151
Some arrests for treason?

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:35.254
Or maybe you'd like
our Obama Netflix?"

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.322
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:38.657
But this is dangerous.

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:41.027
The President is threatening
arrest and imprisonment

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.362
for people who dare to
investigate his abuse of power.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:45.999
The only thing stopping
our system from collapsing

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.900
is that everyone
just ignores him.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.035
We've all gotten to the point
where we have to treat

00:02:50.035 --> 00:02:51.437
the President
of the United States

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.239
like a guy taking a [bleep]
in the subway car.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.576
At some point,
everyone's just gonna move

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.544
to the other end of the country.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.345
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:03.315
By the way, the President

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.584
accusing a sitting congressman
of treason

00:03:05.584 --> 00:03:09.389
simply for investigating him is
itself an impeachable offense.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:12.658
He keeps stacking offenses
on top of impeachable offenses.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:15.695
He's making a Scooby sandwich
of crimes.

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.030
"Scoob, we're about to
get impeached!

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.566
We gotta get outta here!"

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.669
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.706
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.642
It was a...

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.779
It was cartoon that aired
when my writers were young.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:37.316
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:39.952
And as Trump was melting down
this weekend,

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.322
the White House
was dispatching allies

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.857
to the Sunday shows
to try to defend him.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.159
Let's start with the creepiest
member of Trump's staff,

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.995
White House senior policy
advisor Stephen Miller.

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:51.496
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:03:51.496 --> 00:03:54.033
[ Women cackling evilly ]

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:59.305
Miller went on "Fox News Sunday"
right after Fox reported

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.907
that Trump had been in contact

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:03.543
not just with his personal
lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.712
but with two other
private attorneys

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.146
to dig up dirt from Ukraine.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.249
Fox host Chris Wallace
asked Miller why,

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.184
if it was such
a legitimate inquiry,

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.385
Trump didn't go through
official channels,

00:04:13.385 --> 00:04:15.187
and Miller had no answer.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.857
-Why did he use
three private lawyers

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.694
to get information on Biden
from the Ukrainian government

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:24.998
rather than go through all of
the agencies of his government?

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.666
-Two different points.
Number one --

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.201
-How about answering
my question?

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.336
Stephen, I'm asking you
a direct question.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:33.372
Why did the President
use private attorneys

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:34.940
rather than go
to the State Department?

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.742
If you don't know,
that's an acceptable answer.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.644
-There's two issues
that were brought up --

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.646
-I'm now asking two issues.
Why did he do it?

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.114
-Chris, I understand.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:44.083
I understand that you have your
question. I have my answer.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.418
There's two issues that were
brought up on the phone call.

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.253
-You have your nonanswer.
It doesn't work.

00:04:48.253 --> 00:04:51.124
-Damn. Damn, Chris. Be careful.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:54.026
If you anger him too much, he'll
sneak into your room at night,

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.294
bite you on the neck,

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.828
and turn you
into whatever he is,

00:04:56.828 --> 00:04:59.064
which I guess is a...

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.400
hairless cat?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.870
Then there was Ohio Congressman
Jim Jordan,

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.372
who went on CNN
to repeat a bunch

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.407
of debunked conspiracy theories
about Joe Biden.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:11.310
Now, the short version
of what you need to know here

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.613
is that the Obama administration
and most of the West

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:17.249
called for a Ukrainian
prosecutor to be fired

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:20.586
because he wasn't doing enough
to investigate corruption.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:23.655
That prosecutor was not
investigating Biden's son
at the time,

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:25.524
and yet Jordan kept
repeating the lie anyway

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:27.393
until CNN host Jake Tapper
had enough.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.828
-He's getting paid $50,000,
and then when the company

00:05:29.828 --> 00:05:32.364
that's paying him that money
is under investigation,

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:34.267
guess what. Daddy comes
running to the rescue.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.035
The vice president
of the United States --

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.603
-That's not what happened.

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:39.805
Sir, sir.
That's not what happened.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.941
-I'm just telling you
what happened. Joe Biden...

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.742
-No, you're not.
-...called up and said,

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:45.344
"Fire this prosecutor,
or you're not getting..."

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.680
-No, you're suggesting that
Biden called for the prosecutor

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.450
to be fired to protect his son.
That's not what happened.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.320
Joe Biden was trying
to get a prosecutor

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.156
who was not pursuing corruption
fired.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.491
-It's amazing the gymnastics
you guys will go through

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.227
to defend what --

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.928
-Sir, it's not gymnastics.
It's facts.

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.998
-It's fun to see Jake Tapper
tell an actual congressman,

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.901
"This isn't gymnastics."
"What? It isn't? I was about to

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.737
tell a lie while doing
a handstand on a pommel horse."

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:13.606
Sunday was filled
with Republicans

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.675
flailing in one interview
after another

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.776
because they have
no convincing answers

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:19.278
for the President's behavior.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.947
Of course, Rudy was
in the middle of it,

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.448
as he always is.

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.049
Now, given that
he was the key figure

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:26.018
relaying information
between Trump and Ukraine,

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.286
today three different
House committees subpoenaed him.

00:06:28.286 --> 00:06:29.655
On Sunday, Rudy was asked

00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:31.924
if he would comply
with such a subpoena,

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.993
and his answer, as usual,
made no sense.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.728
-Are you going to cooperate

00:06:35.728 --> 00:06:37.630
with the House
Intelligence Committee?

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.400
-That is a question that has
a lot, a lot of implications.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.102
Believe it or not,
I'm an attorney.

00:06:44.102 --> 00:06:46.205
-I do not believe it.

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:49.976
I think -- I think
you are a bunch of body parts

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:53.378
sewn together and brought
to life in a laboratory,

00:06:53.378 --> 00:06:54.814
and maybe, just maybe,

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:58.817
some of the body parts
were from attorneys.

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:00.652
But, by far, my favorite
Republican dumb guy

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:01.887
from the Sunday shows yesterday

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.589
was House Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy,

00:07:03.589 --> 00:07:05.258
who did an interview
with "60 Minutes."

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:08.060
McCarthy was asked about the
notes from Trump's phone call

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.429
with the president of Ukraine.
Now, in these notes,

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:12.598
the president of Ukraine
expressed an interest

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:15.701
in getting more military aid
from the U.S.,

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.036
including anti-tank weapons
called Javelins.

00:07:18.036 --> 00:07:20.105
And immediately after that,
Trump said,

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:22.408
"I would like you
to do us a favor, though."

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:24.477
And when McCarthy was asked
about that exchange,

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:26.311
which seems like
an obvious quid pro quo,

00:07:26.311 --> 00:07:28.847
he tried a very dumb defense
that did not work.

00:07:28.847 --> 00:07:30.849
-What do you make
of this exchange?

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:32.718
President Zelensky says,

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.187
"We are almost ready
to buy more Javelins

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:38.257
from the United States
for defense purposes."

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.058
And President Trump replies,

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:43.396
"I would like you
to do us a favor, though."

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:46.198
-You just added another word.
-No, it's in the transcript.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.568
-He said, "I'd like you
to do a favor, though"?

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:51.637
-Yes, it's in
the White House transcript.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.072
-I mean, it's ama--

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:55.707
I love that his genius defense
was, "You added a word."

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:57.143
And it wasn't even true.

00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:59.911
Also, which word
in that sentence does he think

00:07:59.911 --> 00:08:03.715
if you took it out
would suddenly make it okay?

00:08:03.715 --> 00:08:05.851
But my favorite part
of the interview came next

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.086
when "60 Minutes" host
Scott Pelley asked McCarthy

00:08:08.086 --> 00:08:10.523
how he planned
to defend the President.

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:13.058
-How do you expect
the President's defense

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:15.994
to roll out going forward?

00:08:15.994 --> 00:08:18.363
-The defense of what?

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:20.833
-Well, there's an
impeachment inquiry.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.202
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.080
-[Bleep].

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.616
He's like a kid who's stumped
during a spelling bee.

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:40.752
"Impeachment? Uh, can you
use it in a sentence?"

00:08:40.752 --> 00:08:42.488
"Impeachment.
As in, the President

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:45.056
is about to go through
impeachment."

00:08:45.056 --> 00:08:47.726
"Okay. Can you, uh...

00:08:47.726 --> 00:08:50.262
Can you spell it?"

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:52.164
Trump and his allies
can't defend their behavior

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.398
because there is no defense.

00:08:53.398 --> 00:08:55.100
What happened here
is very simple and obvious.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.702
The President asked
for a quid pro quo,

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.236
the White House
tried to cover it up,

00:08:58.236 --> 00:08:59.471
and they got caught.
That's it.

00:08:59.471 --> 00:09:01.640
So now Trump is just lying
about the whistleblower,

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.542
whose report was deemed credible
and urgent

00:09:03.542 --> 00:09:05.577
and corroborated by the notes
from the call itself.

00:09:05.577 --> 00:09:06.979
Today, Trump tweeted,

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.814
"The whistleblower
knew almost nothing.

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:11.217
Its second-hand description
of the call is a fraud."

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.751
Oh, so now
you're suddenly concerned

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:14.186
about second-hand information,

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.021
because you're the guy
who tweeted,

00:09:16.021 --> 00:09:18.323
"An 'extremely credible source'
has called my office and told me

00:09:18.323 --> 00:09:20.826
that Barack Obama's
birth certificate is a fraud."

00:09:20.826 --> 00:09:24.296
You just made that fake source
up for a racist lie.

00:09:24.296 --> 00:09:26.799
Trump likes to think
he's a whistleblower.

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:30.368
That's why his lips
always look like that.

00:09:30.368 --> 00:09:34.106
But in reality,
he's just eating the whistle.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:36.342
"It's pretty cool, actually,

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:38.811
because now when I fart,
it sounds like this...

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:41.013
[ Whistle blows ]

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:45.417
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.417 --> 00:09:48.587
There's another one
coming soon."

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:50.956
In a way, we're lucky that these
guys are incompetent morons

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:52.658
because now rather
than sticking together

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:54.760
and coming up with a coherent
and believable defense,

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.528
they're all pointing fingers
at each other,

00:09:56.528 --> 00:09:58.864
trying to blame one another
for what happened with Ukraine.

00:09:58.864 --> 00:10:01.200
Like Rudy, you know,
the guy who always looks like

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.468
he just woke up in the middle
of every interview.

00:10:03.468 --> 00:10:06.738
I mean, look at him. He looks
like an animatronic robot

00:10:06.738 --> 00:10:08.540
in Disney's
Country Bear Jamboree

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.043
who magically comes to life
when you ask him a question.

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:13.578
Now, last week,
Rudy went on Fox News

00:10:13.578 --> 00:10:16.581
and said it was actually
the State Department

00:10:16.581 --> 00:10:19.218
that instructed him
to pressure Ukraine

00:10:19.218 --> 00:10:22.220
to investigate Joe Biden,
even holding up his phone

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.289
to show the calls
from the State Department.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.725
And then on Thursday night,
he went on Fox News again

00:10:26.725 --> 00:10:28.527
and showed everyone
his text messages

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:31.096
with a State Department official
named Kurt Volker,

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:33.732
who had instructed him to meet
with Ukrainian officials.

00:10:33.732 --> 00:10:35.835
-What is the significance
of these?

00:10:35.835 --> 00:10:37.636
And are you, Rudy, concerned

00:10:37.636 --> 00:10:43.241
that you're unnecessarily
dragging his name into this?

00:10:43.241 --> 00:10:46.612
-Who? Whose name?
-Volker's name.

00:10:46.612 --> 00:10:51.149
-He should step forward
and explain what he did.

00:10:51.149 --> 00:10:55.854
The whistleblower
falsely alleges

00:10:55.854 --> 00:10:57.889
that I was operating on my own.

00:10:57.889 --> 00:11:00.893
Well, I wasn't operating
on my own.

00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:03.562
-I like that Rudy is trying
to smear the whistleblower

00:11:03.562 --> 00:11:06.699
by pointing out the crimes
they didn't report.

00:11:06.699 --> 00:11:08.601
"The whistleblower says
I acted alone.

00:11:08.601 --> 00:11:10.569
Well, joke's on them.
We had a whole team.

00:11:10.569 --> 00:11:12.237
It was like 'Ocean's 11'

00:11:12.237 --> 00:11:15.641
but if they were dumb
and not handsome."

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:18.444
Then Rudy literally pulled out
his iPad -- his iPad --

00:11:18.444 --> 00:11:20.379
and read the text messages
from Volker,

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:21.747
the State Department official

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:23.916
telling him to meet
with Ukrainian officials.

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:27.686
-Well, here's Kurt.
Here's Kurt saying, "Great.

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:30.756
I will tell Yermak, and he'll
visit with you there. Thanks."

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:33.492
"Mr. Mayor, how was
your meeting with Andrei?

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:37.329
Do you have time for a call?
Best, Kurt."

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:40.865
They were all over me
asking me to do it.

00:11:40.865 --> 00:11:42.635
I was happy to do it.

00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:44.970
-Oh, my God. Rudy, you're
literally reading evidence

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.907
against yourself
on national television.

00:11:48.907 --> 00:11:52.044
Look, I'm not a lawyer,
but here's my best legal advice.

00:11:52.044 --> 00:11:53.645
Go back to sleep.

00:11:53.645 --> 00:11:54.980
There you go.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.982
Also, it's never good
when a confused old man

00:11:57.982 --> 00:12:00.085
reads texts off his iPad.

00:12:00.085 --> 00:12:02.321
I mean, best-case scenario,

00:12:02.321 --> 00:12:03.989
it's your grandpa
asking you how to advance

00:12:03.989 --> 00:12:05.724
to the next level
on Candy Crush.

00:12:05.724 --> 00:12:07.359
I want to buy more lives,

00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:10.662
but I keep accidentally
taking pictures of myself."

00:12:10.662 --> 00:12:13.098
But the weirdest part
was when Rudy was asked

00:12:13.098 --> 00:12:15.601
about Republicans
like Utah Senator Mitt Romney,

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:17.937
who had called the Ukraine
accusations troubling,

00:12:17.937 --> 00:12:21.040
and somehow ended up doing a
bizarre impression of Al Gore.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.708
-One time,
Bill Clinton asked me,

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.610
"What's this guy Romney like?"

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:27.646
You know what I told him?
"He's our Al Gore."

00:12:27.646 --> 00:12:29.782
-All right.
Rudy, hold that thought.

00:12:29.782 --> 00:12:32.351
-What do you mean,
"hold that thought"?

00:12:32.351 --> 00:12:35.253
That's not a thought.
That's a spasm.

00:12:35.253 --> 00:12:36.888
I mean, look at him.

00:12:36.888 --> 00:12:40.259
It's like how your grandpa
dances at a wedding.

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.728
He looks like a guy
who's duct-taped to a chair

00:12:42.728 --> 00:12:45.063
trying to break free...

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.765
which is probably something
he's actually done

00:12:46.765 --> 00:12:48.967
because I'm pretty sure after
he does one of these interviews,

00:12:48.967 --> 00:12:51.036
the White House tries
to duct-tape him to a chair

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:53.171
so he can't do another one.

00:12:53.171 --> 00:12:56.274
"Gotta get out of here, Rudy!

00:12:56.274 --> 00:12:57.943
You gotta get loose!

00:12:57.943 --> 00:13:02.314
Gotta go back on TV
and confess to crimes!"

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:04.516
Now, today we found out
that Secretary of State

00:13:04.516 --> 00:13:06.385
Mike Pompeo was, himself,
on the call.

00:13:06.385 --> 00:13:08.720
These guys are all unraveling
and pointing fingers

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.556
at each other because
everything's coming out now.

00:13:10.556 --> 00:13:12.858
For example,
remember that infamous meeting

00:13:12.858 --> 00:13:15.661
Trump had with the Russians
in the Oval Office in 2017?

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:18.564
That was the meeting where
he shared classified information

00:13:18.564 --> 00:13:22.334
and bragged about firing
former FBI director James Comey.

00:13:22.334 --> 00:13:24.636
Well, over the weekend,
"The Washington Post" reported

00:13:24.636 --> 00:13:26.939
that during that meeting,
Trump also told the Russians

00:13:26.939 --> 00:13:29.808
he didn't care that they'd
interfered in the 2016 election,

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:31.977
and then his aides tried
to cover that up, too.

00:13:31.977 --> 00:13:33.679
And then late this afternoon,
we found out

00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:36.048
he also asked the prime minister
of Australia to get involved.

00:13:36.048 --> 00:13:39.551
-President Trump has asked
another foreign leader --

00:13:39.551 --> 00:13:42.421
this time it was the prime
minister of Australia --

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:44.856
to help investigate
his conspiracy theories

00:13:44.856 --> 00:13:48.626
around the origins of the now
complete, over, and shuttered

00:13:48.626 --> 00:13:50.095
Mueller investigation.

00:13:50.095 --> 00:13:51.897
From that "New York Times"
story,

00:13:51.897 --> 00:13:54.299
"President Trump pushed
the Australian prime minister

00:13:54.299 --> 00:13:57.702
during a recent telephone call
to help A.G. William Barr

00:13:57.702 --> 00:14:00.639
gather information for
a Justice Department inquiry

00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:02.073
that Mr. Trump hopes

00:14:02.073 --> 00:14:03.975
will discredit
the Mueller investigation.

00:14:03.975 --> 00:14:06.111
-It keeps happening.
Trump tells a foreign country

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:08.246
he either wants them
to interfere in our elections

00:14:08.246 --> 00:14:09.447
or he doesn't care if they do

00:14:09.447 --> 00:14:11.016
and then his aides
try to hide it.

00:14:11.016 --> 00:14:13.152
Honestly, I'm just shocked
we didn't find out about it

00:14:13.152 --> 00:14:15.520
from a text message on Fox News.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.256
"Rudy, I told the Russians
I don't care

00:14:17.256 --> 00:14:18.790
if they interfere
in our election.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.492
I also asked Australia
to help us out.

00:14:20.492 --> 00:14:23.094
And I tried to bribe Ukraine.
All of this is impeachable.

00:14:23.094 --> 00:14:24.929
Whatever you do,
don't read this text message

00:14:24.929 --> 00:14:27.232
out loud on Fox News."

00:14:27.232 --> 00:14:29.501
[ Laughter ]

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:31.035
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:31.035 --> 00:14:32.604
You can tell...

00:14:32.604 --> 00:14:34.939
impeachment is already having
an impact because rather than

00:14:34.939 --> 00:14:37.209
sticking together and coming up
with a coherent defense,

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:39.578
Trump and his allies are running
through the dumbest excuses

00:14:39.578 --> 00:14:41.346
and pointing fingers
at each other.

00:14:41.346 --> 00:14:43.515
I don't know if this
whole thing will end up

00:14:43.515 --> 00:14:45.650
with anyone getting taken away
in handcuffs,

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:49.688
but if it does, at least we know
what that will look like.

00:14:49.688 --> 00:14:52.091
This has been "A Closer Look."

